  "ownership_scope": "Product-owned debugger_audit_memory and debugger_audit_durable integration targets use the original product audit oracle directly, without either language facade. Nine memory and fifteen SQLite tests run under leserpent-vm. The six SQLite-specific corruption, peer-cache/replay and race bodies move unchanged out of the compatibility facade. Shared oracle code is unchanged. Product default-disabled tests need neither SQLite nor language compatibility crates.",
  "compatibility_scope": "The released leselang-vm HIR/VM paths retain nine memory and nine SQLite wrappers using that same product-owned oracle. Storage mutation and thread-race bodies no longer live in those wrappers. CI explicitly runs direct product acceptance and legacy compatibility; SQLite integration requires the sqlite-journal feature. No library API, default feature, type identity, journal format or runtime behavior changes.",
  "verification_scope": "Before migration the original suites passed 24 tests. Direct product suites pass the identical test-name multiset, plus 18 retained compatibility runs and both nine-case memory-only configurations. Execution totals overlap and are not new language features. Local macOS verification only; CI YAML and both target commands were checked, not run on a remote worker. Native checkpoint contents remain identical and do not include any product audit suite.",
  "remaining_boundaries": [
    "Complete declared-language and reference compatibility acceptance.",
    "Independent host-neutral production durability, real GUI/FFI integrations and physical repository extraction."
  ],
